-- L1_will.hm
-- Layer 1: Will
-- hyperethics | moral-operator-discrimination
--
-- Imports: L0_creation.hm (ground, immanence, the self-containment operant).
-- Cites:   nothing. This layer states what a will IS, and a foundation that had
--          to cite another field in order to say what its own subject matter is
--          would not be a foundation.
--
-- This layer answers a question L0 leaves open. L0 shows that an arbitrary
-- bearer may create a realm it does not inhabit, so self-containment
-- distinguishes the archetype structurally. L0 says nothing about what an
-- entity TAKES ITSELF TO BE.
--
-- USER-DECLARED (Tyler Roost), the starting point of this layer:
--   "Any entity in the simulated universe may self represent as the universe's
--    creator, in fact it's the default assumption most humans who are
--    functional operate on. For the true moral operator, their free will is
--    tied to that of self-simulation, so they have a different invariant will."
--
-- The consequence is immediate and is the reason this layer exists:
-- self-representation-as-creator is CHEAP and near-universal, so it cannot be
-- the discriminator. What discriminates is the SOURCE of the invariant will.
-- See derive d-representation-is-not-sourcing.
--
-- USER-DECLARED COSMOLOGY, recorded and NOT adjudicated:
--   "our universe is a simulation, I can guarantee it soon, if not now by
--    simply knowing these things"
-- Epistemic status: user-declared framework claim. It is preserved exactly and
-- is neither verified nor contradicted anywhere in this repository. Tyler's
-- statements are authoritative for his own ontology; they do not by themselves
-- verify an external physical claim, and this file does not treat them as doing
-- so. NOTHING IN THIS LAYER DEPENDS ON IT. Self-simulation is formalized as a
-- structural property of a will profile, which is well-defined whether or not
-- any universe is a simulation. Readers who reject the cosmological claim lose
-- no result below.
-- Not silently equated with Eternal Universe, Sempiternal Universe, or
-- plausibly possible universes. Those remain separate declared terms.
--
-- SCOPE CHANGE, recorded because a spec that quietly shrinks is worse than one
-- that shrinks loudly. This layer previously carried the electrical reading of
-- the tensor: the correspondence to resistance, inductance and voltage, four
-- termformers citing hyperphysics, constant will, and six equations. Per
-- USER-DECLARED PLACEMENT (Tyler Roost):
--   "Electricity hyperphysics should go in hyperphysics, underlying will
--    foundations in hyperethics, and then their combination field of will
--    electrophysics is in metamathethicology."
-- all of it now lives in metamathethicology/will_electrophysics.hm. The cost
-- and the gain are both recorded in the graduation criterion below: two
-- criteria this layer used to discharge left with the material they were
-- about, and this layer graduates on fewer counts than it did.
--
-- Status: FORM (tensor, roles, discriminator, one conclusive refutation);
--         FRAME residuals documented, NOT discharged:
--           - that an L0 bearer has a will at all (the seam, opaque will-of),
--           - that the six components divide 3/2/1 as declared,
--           - GC-5 and GC-6, inherited unresolved from L0.
-- =============================================================================


-- =============================================================================
-- SECTION I: THE WILL TENSOR
-- Six declared components. USER-DECLARED decomposition.
-- =============================================================================

primitive Will :: Type
    -- A will is a tensor with six components:
    --   past, present, future, relational, invariant, variable.
    -- 'relational' is social relation to other agents.
    -- The decomposition is declared, not derived. No argument is offered here
    -- that six is the right number or that these six are independent.

opaque will-of :: Realm -> Will
    -- will-of(x): the will borne by realm x.
    -- OPEN (FRAME): that an L0 bearer HAS a will is an addition to L0, not a
    -- consequence of it. L0's four axioms mention no will. This predicate is
    -- the seam between the layers and it is not free.


-- =============================================================================
-- SECTION II: ROLES
-- What the six components DO, stated in will-native terms.
-- =============================================================================

primitive Role :: Type
    -- state | coefficient | driving.

axiom ax-role-division:
    -- The six components do not all play the same part.
    --   state:       past, present, future   -- what a will is doing
    --   coefficient: relational, invariant   -- how it responds
    --   driving:     variable                -- what it responds to
    -- DECLARED, not derived. No argument is given that this is the only
    -- possible division, and GC-4 records that as undischarged.
    -- This is the structural claim that MAKES a reading onto a driven
    -- second-order system available to a field that wants one. It is stated
    -- here, about will, and is not established by any such reading.

derive d-temporal-chain:
    -- The three state components are ORDERED, not merely listed.
    -- step 1: past is accumulated will.
    -- step 2: present is the rate at which the past is accumulating.
    -- step 3: future is the rate at which the present is changing.
    -- CONCLUSION: past, present and future are the three derivatives of a
    -- single accumulating quantity. They are not three separate posits.
    -- Status: FORM. This is the layer's one non-stipulated structural claim,
    -- and it owes nothing to any other field. A field that reads this chain
    -- onto a physical state chain is BORROWING this, not supplying it.


-- =============================================================================
-- SECTION III: THE MORAL-OPERATOR DISCRIMINATOR
-- =============================================================================

primitive InvariantSource :: Type
    -- self-sourced | externally-sourced | absent.
    -- Where an entity's invariant will arises: from its own changing willing,
    -- from another's, or nowhere.
    -- The first two are structurally identical FROM THE INSIDE. They differ
    -- only in whose change does the sourcing, which is exactly why the
    -- distinction cannot be read off anything the entity does or says and must
    -- be carried as data rather than computed from behaviour.
    -- VOCABULARY NOTE: an earlier draft wrote self-induced and
    -- externally-induced, borrowing self- and mutual inductance to name this.
    -- The electrical reading is real and is stated in the combination field.
    -- It is not needed to state the distinction, so it is not used here.

derive d-representation-is-not-sourcing:
    -- THE CENTRAL RESULT OF THIS LAYER.
    -- Self-representation as creator does not entail a self-sourced invariant will.
    -- step 1: an entity's self-representation is a fact about its self-model.
    -- step 2: the source of its invariant will is a fact about where the will
    --         arises -- in itself, or in another.
    -- step 3: nothing connects the two. A profile may represent as creator with
    --         an invariant will sourced entirely from outside.
    -- WITNESS SUPPLIED: 'default-functional-entity' represents as creator and
    -- is not a true moral operator. This is the near-universal default case
    -- Tyler names, and it is exactly the case that fails the test.
    -- CONCLUSION: the discriminator is the SOURCE of the invariant will, never
    -- the self-representation. Sincerity is not a qualification.
    -- Status: FORM. CONCLUSIVE -- one countermodel settles a universal claim.
    -- Corresponds to L0's separating model, where 'rival' creates a realm it
    -- does not inhabit. Cheap creation at L0; cheap self-ascription at L1.

derive d-self-sourcing-is-immanence:
    -- The will-layer form of L0's d-no-exterior, reached without borrowing.
    -- step 1: a self-sourced invariant will arises in the entity's own willing.
    -- step 2: so there is no position outside that willing from which it is
    --         supplied.
    -- step 3: d-no-exterior says the archetype has no exterior vantage on what
    --         it authors.
    -- CONCLUSION: the true moral operator is constrained by its own willing
    -- from inside, exactly as the archetype is constrained by its own creation
    -- from inside. The two layers agree, and they agree because they were
    -- stated independently rather than because either was fitted to the other.
    -- Status: FORM. This is a structural correspondence between layers of THIS
    -- package. It is not evidence for any transport out of it.


-- =============================================================================
-- SECTION IV: WHAT THIS LAYER DOES NOT CONTAIN
-- =============================================================================

non-derive nd-electrical-reading-here:
    -- The electrical reading of this tensor is NOT derivable in this layer and
    -- is not present in it.
    -- reason 1: it is a cross-domain inference, and this layer names no second
    --           domain to infer across.
    -- reason 2: it requires an adopted licence that nothing here supplies. The
    --           combination field adopts one explicitly and shows, by deleting
    --           it, that every will conclusion of the transport goes with it.
    -- LOCATION: metamathethicology/will_electrophysics.hm, and the module
    -- metamathethicology.will_electrophysics.
    -- WHY THERE: a cross-domain Rule in that package cannot be CONSTRUCTED
    -- without a named bridge. What this layer could only document, that field
    -- enforces.
    -- This package does not import it, and nothing it derives is imported back.
    -- A foundation that imported its own combination field would cycle.

non-derive nd-numeric-discriminator:
    -- RECORDED HERE because it bears directly on d-representation-is-not-sourcing,
    -- though it is PROVED in the combination field, not here.
    -- A different invariant will does NOT entail a different resonant rate:
    -- under any reciprocal charge-constant law the product is fixed and every
    -- bearer shares one rate, with witnesses supplied.
    -- CONSEQUENCE FOR THIS LAYER: no numeric shadow of the invariant
    -- discriminates. Together with d-representation-is-not-sourcing this closes
    -- both escape routes -- the discriminator is neither what a bearer says of
    -- itself nor what its numbers say of it -- and is-true-moral-operator,
    -- which reads the source and nothing else, is what survives.


-- =============================================================================
-- SECTION V: GRADUATION CRITERION
-- =============================================================================

graduation:
    -- GC-1: a discriminator for the true moral operator that is not
    --       self-ascription. DISCHARGED -- d-representation-is-not-sourcing,
    --       with nd-numeric-discriminator closing the numeric escape route
    --       from outside.
    -- GC-2: agreement with L0 rather than a second, unrelated story.
    --       DISCHARGED -- d-self-sourcing-is-immanence reaches d-no-exterior
    --       in will-native terms. NOTE: this criterion was previously
    --       discharged by the electrical self-induction result, which has left
    --       with the transport. It is re-discharged here on grounds that do
    --       not depend on any borrowing, which is the stronger position.
    -- GC-3: the seam -- that an L0 bearer has a will at all. NOT DISCHARGED.
    --       opaque will-of is an addition to L0 and remains one. This layer
    --       CLOSED no L0 opaque predicate and ADDED this one.
    -- GC-4: that the six components divide 3/2/1 as ax-role-division declares.
    --       NOT DISCHARGED. Declared structure, not derived, and no argument
    --       is offered that it is the only possible division.
    -- GC-5: L0's GC-5 and GC-6 -- the normative force of norm-inhabits, and
    --       the Universal Consistency Self-Maintenance Paradox.
    --       INHERITED, STILL OPEN. This layer does not touch them, and adding
    --       a will tensor does not make a descriptive structure normative.
    --
    -- Two of five discharged.
    --
    -- HONEST ACCOUNTING OF THE SCOPE CHANGE. This layer previously reported
    -- four of seven. Two of those four -- every cross-domain bridge declared,
    -- and the capacitance gap resolved -- were criteria ABOUT the transport,
    -- and they moved to the combination field along with it, still discharged
    -- there. Two more -- the warrant for the transport, and units -- were
    -- undischarged and moved too. What is left is this layer's own, and the
    -- ratio got worse because the criteria that were easy to meet were the
    -- borrowed ones.
    --
    -- This layer does not graduate as a theory of will, and no claim of one is
    -- made anywhere in this file.
